{
  "version": "r0a-errors-v3",
  "rules": [
    "Public responses only use codes listed in public; unknown internal failures map to service_degraded.",
    "message is safe display text; it never echoes goal, background, title or artifact content.",
    "Worker-only database exceptions map to service_degraded on the public API and keep the raw code in internal logs.",
    "retryable means the same request may be resent unchanged: true only for 5xx and 429. preview_stale is not retryable; the client must create a new preview (recovery_action re_preview).",
    "db_exception_map lists every RAISE EXCEPTION code in r0a-schema-draft.sql (prefix before \":\"), including public codes raised verbatim; entries no longer raised are removed."
  ],
